   "name": "Equivalent Fractions",
   "definition": null
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "Equivalent Fractions"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "What are equivalent fractions?"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- **Equivalent** **fractions **are two fractions that represent the **same amount**\n\n  - They are different ways of writing the same thing\n  - For example, $\\frac{1}{2}$ and $\\frac{6}{12}$ are equivalent fractions"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "How do I find an equivalent fraction?"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- To find an equivalent fraction, **multiply the top and bottom** of a fraction by the same number\n\n  - $\\frac{5}{6}$ is equivalent to $\\frac{5\\times2}{6\\times2}=\\frac{10}{12}$ and $\\frac{5\\times3}{6\\times3}=\\frac{15}{18}$ and $\\frac{5\\times4}{6\\times4}=\\frac{20}{24}$etc.\n  - For each fraction, there are an **infinite number **of equivalent fractions"
  },
  {
   "type": "spec_point",
   "id": "spcpt_hd6mC5SC7tP26krr",
   "name": "Simplifying Fractions",
   "definition": null
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "Simplifying Fractions"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "What is a simplified fraction?"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- A **simplified fraction** is a fraction that is written using the **smallest **possible ***integer***** values**\n\n  - Simplifying turns a fraction into an 'easier' **equivalent fraction**\n- If both the numerator and denominator can be divided by the **same number** (called a ***common factor***), the fraction can be **simplified**\n- Simplifying is also called **cancelling** a fraction"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "How do I simplify fractions?"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- To simplify the fraction,** divide the top and bottom **by the common factor"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- $\\frac{12}{18}=\\frac{12\\div6}{18\\div6}=\\frac{2}{3}$\n- $\\frac{25}{45}=\\frac{25\\div5}{45\\div5}=\\frac{5}{9}$"
  },
  {
   "type": "callout",
   "variant": "exam-tip",
   "label": "Exam Hint",
   "md": "- Make use of your calculator\n\n  - Type any fraction into it and pressing equals will automatically simplify the fraction for you"
  }
 ]
